## 1. Architektur-Übersicht

### High-Level Design
```
Bootstrap Scene (Initialization)
    ↓
Outside Scene (Main Gameplay)
    ↓
House_Interior, Farm, etc. (weitere Szenen via DoorTrigger)
```

### Ordnerstruktur
```
Scripts/
├── Camera/          - Kamera-Steuerung & Follow-System
├── Input/           - Input-Handling & Services
├── Interactions/    - Interaktions-System (IItemUseHandler, Interactable)
├── Inventory/       - Inventar-Datenstrukturen (InventorySlot)
├── Items/           - Item-System, Drops, ItemTemplate
├── Manager/         - Zentrale Manager (UI, Transitions, etc.)
│   └── UI/          - UI-spezifische Manager
├── Player/          - Player-Logik (Movement, Interact, Input)
├── Scenes/          - Szenen-spezifische Skripte (Doors, SpawnPoints, MainMenu)
├── UI/              - UI-Komponenten (SlotView, Tabs, Panels)
└── WorldObjects/    - Interaktive Objekte (Trees, Items)
    └── SpecificObjects/ - Spezifische Implementierungen (Tree.cs)
```

### Core Patterns
- **Singleton**: Player, Manager (via BootStrapper)
- **Service Pattern**: InputService, DropSystem
- **Event-Driven**: Input, Inventory, HotBar kommunizieren via C# Events
- **DontDestroyOnLoad**: Alle Manager, Player und UI_Root bleiben persistent über Szenen
- **Interface-Based Interaction**: IItemUseHandler für Tool-System

